{"availability":"available","full":"rootform-dev/rootform","name":"rootform","description":"Rootform distribution, public contracts, documentation, and examples","category":"Developer tools","language":"HCL","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-30T21:24:51Z","updated":"2026-10-04T07:43:36Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"dev","homepage":null,"topics":["architecture","documentation","infrastructure-as-code","rootform","terraform"],"demo":"https://rootform.dev/playground/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:01.397Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:01.397Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:01.397Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:16:01.397Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Rootform reads plan and state exports from Terraform or OpenTofu, then shows the architecture they describe: which resources sit where and what connects to what. Plans also show what changes. It reads exported state the same way, for a snapshot of the architecture recorded in state. The result is a Form, a saved file you can explore in a browser, question from the terminal, compare with another revision, and check against Policies. Every placement and connection is a fact a Dialect Rule established from the export; when a value is unknown until apply, Rootform says so instead of guessing.","Rootform never runs Terraform or OpenTofu, executes providers, or contacts a cloud account. It reads the exported plan or state JSON locally.","Try it without installing anything in the Playground, then follow the quickstart."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rootform-dev/rootform/blob/dev/README.md","fingerprint":"080dbaea904d70bc635d28a2bf49e3db2f01054e6cca85729c4f092430326bac","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:38.568Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:38.568Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Rootform reads plan and state exports from Terraform or OpenTofu, then shows the architecture they describe: which resources sit where and what connects to what. Plans also show what changes. It reads exported state the same way, for a snapshot of the architecture recorded in state. The result is a Form, a saved file you can explore in a browser, question from the terminal, compare with another revision, and check against Policies. Every placement and connection is a fact a Dialect Rule established from the export; when a value is unknown until apply, Rootform says so instead of guessing.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rootform-dev/rootform/blob/dev/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"080dbaea904d70bc635d28a2bf49e3db2f01054e6cca85729c4f092430326bac","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rootform-dev/rootform/blob/dev/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:38.568Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T07:43:36Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rootform-dev/rootform/blob/dev/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:38.568Z","hash":"080dbaea904d70bc635d28a2bf49e3db2f01054e6cca85729c4f092430326bac","originalBytes":7439,"storedBytes":7439,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["rootform","docs","form","license","policy","plan","state","dialects","examples","plan.tfplan","run","terraform","architecture","evidence","export","json","plan.json","analysis.json","cli","explorer","head","what","bash","check","contracts","explain","explore","integrations","never","playground","result","saved","against","analyze","cloud","commands","compare","does","every","index.md","install","instead","keep","lists","module","no-serve","official","out","plan-file","policy-packs","reads","reports","repository","rule","show","state.json","synthetic","where","add","base","baseline","binary","choose","command","commerce-platform","completed","connection","contain","data","dialect","diff","distributed","documentation","each","established","evaluates","evaluation","exit","exported","facts","forms","images","live","loop